  "content": {
    "id": "p21-q12-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "12",
    "prompt": "We will solve $\\dfrac{x}{6}\\ge\\dfrac{1}{|x-5|}$ without a graph by considering cases.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p21-q12-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "Show that $x|x-5|\\ge6$.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x|x-5|\\ge6$.",
          "worked": "The original inequality requires $x\\ne5$, so $|x-5|>0$. Multiplying both sides by the positive quantity $6|x-5|$ preserves the inequality:\n$$x|x-5|\\ge6.$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 18
      },
      {
        "id": "p21-q12-b",
        "type": "group",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "Consider $|x-5|$ as the piecewise function:\n$$|x-5|=\\begin{cases}x-5,&\\text{for }x\\ge5,\\\\-(x-5),&\\text{for }x<5.\\end{cases}$$\nTherefore, remove the absolute value signs and solve $x|x-5|\\ge6$:\n(you will need to use quadratic inequalities)",
        "layout": "grid",
        "columns": 2,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [
          {
            "id": "p21-q12-b-case-ge5",
            "type": "part",
            "label": "",
            "prompt": "$x\\ge5$",
            "layout": "list",
            "columns": null,
            "questionDiagrams": [],
            "children": [],
            "answer": {
              "short": "$x\\ge6$.",
              "worked": "$$\\begin{aligned}x(x-5)&\\ge6\\\\x^2-5x-6&\\ge0\\\\(x-6)(x+1)&\\ge0\\end{aligned}$$\nHence $x\\le-1$ or $x\\ge6$. The case requires $x\\ge5$, so $x\\le-1$ is rejected and $x\\ge6$ remains.",
              "solutionDiagrams": []
            },
            "answerSpaceMm": 38
          },
          {
            "id": "p21-q12-b-case-lt5",
            "type": "part",
            "label": "",
            "prompt": "$x<5$:",
            "layout": "list",
            "columns": null,
            "questionDiagrams": [],
            "children": [],
            "answer": {
              "short": "$2\\le x\\le3$.",
              "worked": "$$\\begin{aligned}-x(x-5)&\\ge6\\\\-x^2+5x-6&\\ge0\\\\x^2-5x+6&\\le0\\\\(x-2)(x-3)&\\le0\\end{aligned}$$\nThus $2\\le x\\le3$, which satisfies $x<5$.",
              "solutionDiagrams": []
            },
            "answerSpaceMm": 38
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p21-q12-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "Explain why $x\\le-1$ is not a solution to the inequality.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "It contradicts the case condition $x\\ge5$ under which it was obtained.",
          "worked": "The result $x\\le-1$ was obtained using $|x-5|=x-5$, which applies only when $x\\ge5$. No value can satisfy both $x\\le-1$ and $x\\ge5$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 11
      },
      {
        "id": "p21-q12-d",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "d",
        "prompt": "Therefore, state the solution to the inequality $\\dfrac{x}{6}\\ge\\dfrac{1}{|x-5|}$.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$2\\le x\\le3$ or $x\\ge6$.",
          "worked": "Combining the valid results from the two cases gives $2\\le x\\le3$ or $x\\ge6$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 10
      }
    ]
  },
